; less.grid - less paging a 500-line file inside the alternate screen.
; Audited against corpus/less.bin. Frames 1, 2 and 9 sit on the alternate-screen transitions and
; are legitimately blank - the normal screen is cleared at start-up and never written again. The
; six interval samples are what pin the paging itself; frame 3 deliberately cuts mid-line ("row"
; rather than "row 20"), which is the state a correct engine holds part-way through a read.
; The inverse-video status line is style 'a' in the frames that show it.
; No divergent path is exercised.
;
; Ported to the unified seam. The header key that lists wrapped rows is now 'continues', and
; ITerminalGrid.ContinuesPreviousRow(N) is true for the row that continues the one above it -
; the direction the engine already stores, and the only direction that is answerable for the
; bottom viewport row. The rows listed are exactly the ones this file has always listed, so the
; audited wrap points are unchanged; the key was renamed so that a file written under the
; earlier 'wrapped' key cannot be mistaken for one written under this one.
;
; Corrected 2026-08-28: every cursor line here read 'steady', which was the engine reporting a
; TerminalOptions field nothing ever wrote (gap 11) and not audited terminal behaviour. The
; power-on cursor style is a blinking block - DECSCUSR Ps=0 and Ps=1 both name it as the default -
; and corpus/less.bin contains no DECSCUSR and no DEC mode 12, so the cursor blinks for the whole
; of this recording. All nine frames now read 'blink'.
;
# less  frame 1/9  after 88/1517 bytes  (alt screen enter)
size 120x30
alt on
cursor col=0 row=0 visible shape=block blink
scrollback 0
title "C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\less.exe"
icon "C:\\Program Files\\Git\\usr\\bin\\less.exe"
modes autowrap focus mouse=off/x10 kitty=none
continues none
text
  r00-r29 ~blank~
style
  s00-s29 ~default~
legend
    .  default

